CAT = "iiqeIntermediaries"; SEG = "LIC"
Q = [
("Since 23 September 2019, insurance agents and brokers in Hong Kong have been:",
 "Licensed directly by the IA", ["Registered with self-regulatory bodies", "Authorized by their insurers only", "Exempt from any licensing"],
 "The IA's statutory licensing regime replaced the old self-regulatory system run by the IARB, CIB and PIBA."),
("Which of these is a 'regulated activity' that needs an IA licence when done for reward?",
 "Negotiating an insurance contract", ["Printing a policy document", "Typing data for an insurer", "Delivering mail to an insurer"],
 "Regulated activities are negotiating or arranging contracts, inviting or inducing a person to enter a contract or make a material decision, and giving regulated advice."),
("Advice to a client on whether to surrender a life policy is:",
 "Regulated advice", ["Not regulated, as no sale occurs", "Regulated only for brokers", "Exempt clerical work"],
 "Regulated advice covers applications, renewals, cancellation, surrender or assignment, exercising rights, changing terms and making claims."),
("Direct sales staff employed by an insurer who advise customers on its products:",
 "Need an individual agent licence", ["Are exempt as employees", "Need only a broker licence", "Need no licence if salaried"],
 "The insurer's own exemption does not extend to its staff acting as its representatives, so they need individual insurance agent licences."),
("Which person is exempt from licensing when giving regulated advice?",
 "A solicitor advising in practice", ["An agency's sales manager", "A part-time insurance seller", "A broker's account executive"],
 "Counsel, solicitors, certified public accountants, trust companies and actuaries are among the classes exempt for regulated advice."),
("An individual who carries on regulated activities as an agent of a licensed insurance agency holds a:",
 "Technical representative (agent) licence", ["Individual insurance agent licence", "Technical representative (broker) licence", "Insurance agency licence"],
 "An individual insurance agent acts for an authorized insurer; a technical representative (agent) acts for a licensed insurance agency."),
("Every licensed insurance agency and licensed insurance broker company must appoint at least one:",
 "Responsible officer", ["Appointed actuary", "Compliance auditor", "Data processor"],
 "Each must have at least one IA-approved responsible officer, a licensed technical representative, to supervise compliance with section 90 conduct requirements."),
("Under section 68 of the IO, an insurer that appointed an agent is liable for the agent's acts in dealings with clients:",
 "Even outside the agent's authority", ["Only if within the agent's authority", "Only if the client signed a waiver", "Only for long term business"],
 "Section 68 imposes vicarious liability on the appointing insurer, unless the agent clearly disclosed the lack of authority before the client relied on the act."),
("An agent appointed by two insurers for the same line does something outside the authority of both. Under section 68:",
 "Both, jointly and severally", ["Neither insurer is liable", "Only the first insurer to appoint him", "Only the agent is liable"],
 "Where several appointments cover the line and the act is within none of their authorities, all those insurers are jointly and severally liable."),
("Under the IA's rules, a licensed individual insurance agent may be appointed by at most:",
 "4 insurers, no more than 2 long term", ["2 insurers, of any kind", "6 insurers, no more than 3 long term", "Any number of insurers"],
 "The Insurance (Maximum Number of Authorized Insurers) Rules allow up to 4 authorized insurers, of which no more than 2 may be long term insurers."),
("A licensed technical representative (agent) may at the same time be:",
 "A responsible officer of its agency", ["A TR (agent) of a second agency", "A licensed individual insurance agent", "A licensed TR (broker)"],
 "Responsible officers of an agency must themselves be licensed TRs (agent). A TR (agent) must not act for another agency or also hold an individual agent or TR (broker) licence."),
("A licence applicant for an insurance agency must, among other things, be:",
 "Appointed by an authorized insurer", ["A Hong Kong incorporated company", "A member of the HKFI's board", "Holding a broker licence too"],
 "An agency applicant must be fit and proper, have fit and proper controllers, be appointed by at least one authorized insurer and hold no conflicting licence."),
("In deciding whether a person is fit and proper to be licensed, the IA must have regard to the person's:",
 "Reputation and integrity", ["Family background", "Nationality and place of birth", "Age and gender"],
 "The IO lists education or experience, competence, reputation and integrity, financial status, disciplinary record and related matters."),
("For a company applying to be a licensed broker, a 'controller' includes a person controlling at least what share of the voting power?",
 "15%", ["5%", "10%", "25%"],
 "A controller of a company owns or controls 15% or more of the issued shares or voting rights, or exercises ultimate control over management."),
("Which secondary school result is among the education qualifications for an individual licence?",
 "Level 2 in 5 HKDSE subjects", ["Level 4 in 3 HKDSE subjects", "Any 2 HKDSE subjects", "A pass in English only"],
 "The usual route is Level 2 or above in five HKDSE subjects including Chinese or English Language and Mathematics, or an equivalent qualification."),
("The IA generally expects a proposed responsible officer to have at least:",
 "5 years in insurance, 2 managing", ["10 years in insurance, 5 managing", "2 years in insurance, none managing", "3 years in insurance, 1 managing"],
 "GL23 notes a responsible officer should generally have at least 5 years' industry experience including 2 years of management, plus a degree or specified qualification."),
("An individual licensee must be a Hong Kong permanent resident or:",
 "Hold a visa that allows the work", ["Live in Hong Kong for a year", "Be sponsored by a broker", "Hold a Mainland passport"],
 "GL23 requires a permanent resident, or a person whose immigration visa or permit does not restrict them from regulated activities in Hong Kong."),
("Under section 90 of the IO, a licensed insurance intermediary must exercise the care, skill and diligence of:",
 "A prudent person doing that activity", ["The best expert in the market", "The client's own lawyer", "An ordinary member of the public"],
 "Section 90 sets the standard of a prudent person carrying on the regulated activity, alongside acting honestly, fairly and in the client's best interests."),
("A licensed agent breaches a provision of the IA's Code of Conduct. By itself, this:",
 "May affect whether he is fit and proper", ["Is a criminal offence", "Lets the client sue on the Code itself", "Has no consequence at all"],
 "The codes are not subsidiary legislation, but the IA may take a breach into account in deciding whether the person is fit and proper to remain licensed."),
("Which disciplinary power under section 81 of the IO can the IA use against a licensed intermediary?",
 "Suspending the licence", ["Imprisoning the intermediary", "Cancelling the client's policy", "Seizing the agent's home"],
 "The IA may revoke or suspend a licence, prohibit applications, reprimand publicly or privately, or impose a pecuniary penalty."),
("A licensed broker company must pay premiums it receives from clients into an account that:",
 "Bears the word 'client' in its title", ["Is in the broker's director's name", "Is held at the insurer", "Is shared with the broker's own funds"],
 "Client money goes into at least one client account with an authorized institution in the company's name, titled with the word 'client', reconciled monthly."),
("Which intermediary is required by law to maintain professional indemnity insurance?",
 "A licensed insurance broker company", ["A licensed individual insurance agent", "A licensed technical representative (agent)", "A licensed insurance agency"],
 "Brokers act for the client as experts and must hold PII. Agents need not, as the appointing insurer is vicariously liable for them."),
("Each year, most individual licensees must earn CPD hours that include a minimum number on:",
 "Ethics or regulations", ["Investment returns", "Sales techniques", "Foreign languages"],
 "GL24 requires at least 15 CPD hours each assessment period, of which at least 3 must be on an 'Ethics or Regulations' topic."),
("A CPD assessment period for licensed insurance intermediaries runs from:",
 "1 August to 31 July", ["1 January to 31 December", "1 April to 31 March", "The licence date for 12 months"],
 "Each assessment period runs from 1 August of one year to 31 July of the next; the CPD declaration is due within two months, by 30 September."),
]
